# The daily codebase trend, filed onto a packet (backlog 06048ade).
#
# David, 2026-09-11: "once we have code base analysis statistics that we
# can start to get a sense for whether we are getting simpler and more
# reliable or more complex as we go."
#
# WHY THIS HOST. The measurement reads the first-parent history of main,
# so it needs a git checkout, and this is the box that keeps one current:
# boss-gcp-converge fetches forge main into /opt/boss every thirty
# minutes. The cluster has no checkout, which is why this is a host timer
# and not a CronJob.
#
# WHICH REF, PINNED. `--ref main` rather than the trunk walk
# (forge/main → origin/main → main): remote names are PER CLONE, and in
# THIS checkout `origin` is the public GitHub mirror, which lags the
# forge — 238 commits behind on one measured day. The converge leaves the
# local `main` branch fast-forwarded to forge main and refuses to run at
# all unless the checkout is clean and on main, so `main` here is the
# forge's main by construction. The row also carries `head` and `head_at`,
# so a measurement taken against a stale checkout says how stale it was
# instead of looking current.
[Unit]
Description=BOSS daily codebase metrics (delete:add, registry rows, totals by area)
Documentation=file:/opt/boss/infra/codebase-metrics.sh
Wants=network-online.target
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
# One git pass over ~470 landings plus one archive of the tree: about two
# seconds measured. The ceiling is for a contended box, not the work.
TimeoutStartSec=10min
# THE SYSTEM OF RECORD, PINNED INLINE WITH env(1) on every line that
# speaks to it. deploy-services' shared jobs-url.conf drop-in points this
# host's timer fleet at the legacy 127.0.0.1 instance, drop-in env
# outranks unit Environment=, and that instance has never heard of a
# bundle-only kind: the packet would die 400 in ExecStartPre and the
# measurement would be PATCHed onto an instance nobody reads. Same fix
# the estate observers needed (91ddebfb), and timers-leave-a-packet
# check 7 makes it the rule.
#
# ExecStartPre=- because the packet is VISIBILITY, NEVER A PRECONDITION —
# except that here the packet is also where the work LANDS, so the
# distinction is worth stating: if the API is unreachable the wrap exits
# 0 and lets the run proceed, the run then finds no open packet, prints
# the whole measurement to the journal and exits non-zero. The
# measurement is never lost to a reduction (CLAUDE.md §Diagnosis), and
# the failed unit is a state somebody notices.
ExecStartPre=-/usr/bin/env BOSS_JOBS_URL=http://10.20.0.34:7900 /opt/boss/infra/boss-maintenance-wrap.sh maintenance-codebase-metrics "Codebase metrics"
ExecStart=/usr/bin/env BOSS_JOBS_URL=http://10.20.0.34:7900 /opt/boss/infra/codebase-metrics.sh file --repo /opt/boss --ref main
ExecStopPost=-/usr/bin/env BOSS_JOBS_URL=http://10.20.0.34:7900 /opt/boss/infra/boss-step.sh maintenance-codebase-metrics run
